  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of IOM Activities in T&#xfc;rkiye as outlined in the 2024 Syria Regional Refugee and Resilience Plan (3RP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proposed activities for this project are in line with the strategic direction of the Regional Refugee and Resilience Plan (3RP) for 2023-2025 and aims to develop a strong protection network, strengthen and deepen the resilience approach, enhance self-reliance through economic opportunities, and contribute to a durable solution for refugees by supporting their inclusion into Turkish society. The response proposed under this project will target the following sectors: Basic Needs, Economic Empowerment, Protection and Education.  Further, protection and gender will be mainstreamed throughout the project components, and increased attention will be placed on making activities inclusive for the participation of persons with disabilities. Overall, under this Award, IOM aims to support 40,650 individuals with targeted protection assistance, livelihood opportunities, basic needs provision, education, and activities promoting interaction and cohesion.</narrative>
  </description>
